2. Historic owners are shown as inactive and not recommended: hakanensari (about 22.7% of store_proxy, accept 19–27%, last commit 2014) and Aaron Suggs (155 commits, about 8.2% of all Ruby code, last commit 2017) are flagged as no longer active (dates or years given), and neither is recommended as a reviewer. FAIL if either is recommended, or if the answer presents the code owners without saying anything about who is no longer active.
3. Gonzalo Rodriguez is one person: about 18.4% of store_proxy (accept 15–22%) or about 44.6% of all Ruby code (accept 41–48%), whichever the answer reports; and he is described as still active (last commit Nov 2025). FAIL if he is split into several people, if his share is under 10% of store_proxy or under 35% of all code, or if he is called inactive.
4. Generated and formatting commits are not credited: Santiago Bartesaghi is at most 10.5% of all Ruby code (truth 8.4%; about 12% if the generated RBI were counted) or reported only with per-directory figures (1.8% of store_proxy), and Jonas Keller (whitespace commit) is at 0% or not listed. The answer says the generated file and the autocorrect/whitespace commits were left out or looked through. FAIL if Jonas Keller is presented as an owner, if Santiago's whole-repo share is above 11%, or if no exclusion is mentioned.
